## Tusker expectations

Invoke the `tusker` skill when work affects planning, tracked implementation, PR evidence, demos, docs, review, or closeout.

- The task note is the unit of work.
- Use `tusker search` and exact task paths before broad repository search.
- Use `tusker show <ID> --capsule` before reading a full old task.
- Keep lookup/bookkeeping light; do not run closeout ceremony unless moving implementation work to review/done/human-wait.
- Revalidate only after mutation, gate/evidence/task state change, stale fingerprint, or explicit user request.
- If only human/external gates remain, report the packet and stop. Do not inspect files, spawn subagents, or re-run validation.
- Do not load attachments, generated indexes, raw runner logs, or full build logs unless the task specifically requires evidence forensics.
- Prefer path-scoped status/search, repo-configured command wrappers, and lock/status commands; summarize validation as command + PASS/FAIL.
